<properties>
    <!--
      Defaults, used only when the property does not already exist. Once the
      wearer has set a value - from the on-watch menu or from Garmin Connect -
      that value wins and this file is ignored.

      Grass adds nothing (0% since question 25, 2026-09-23), which is the
      right default: an untouched install shows the API's own number, altered
      only by altitude, rather than a number nobody asked for. Any other surface resets to grass at local midnight.

      "openness" (Surroundings) was removed on 2026-09-23. A watch that had it
      set keeps the orphaned value; nothing reads it.

      Application.Properties.setValue throws InvalidKeyException for a key that
      is not declared here, so every key UvSettings writes must appear below.
    -->
    <property id="surface" type="number">0</property>
</properties>
